    "https://www.angelo.edu/work-at-asu/": {
      "title": "Your Career Path",
      "description": "Employment  · Angelo State University Skip to Main content Angelo State University Search Toggle Search Form Apply Toggle Main Menu Give Your Career Path at ASU Begins Here! At Angelo State, the Ram Family extends beyond our students to include the faculty and staff who support learning and community every day. Academics Academic Programs Departments Colleges Courses Academic Advising Academic Calendar About ASU History Core Values News Traditions About San Angelo Welcome from the President Mission Statement Admissions & Aid Apply to ASU Admitted Students Request More Information Visit Angelo State University Paying for College Life on Campus Live Play Lead Work Explore Community ASU Mayer Museum Alumni Association Small Business Development Center West Texas Collection Natural History Collections Kay Bailey Hutchison Institute Laura W. Bush Institute for Women’s Health Arts at ASU Planetarium Stephens Chapel Ranch and Meat Market ASU Ticket Office Summer Camps and Conferences Give to ASU Make a Gift Signature Events Join Athletics Quick Links RamPort Library Bookstore Events Public Health Updates Administration Research Mental Health Services Title IX/Incident Report En Español Information For Current Students Faculty & Staff Admitted Students Military Parents & Families Alumni Visitors School Counselors Online Students In this section Employment Faculty/Staff Job Postings Student Job Postings ASU Community Benefits Home / Employment Recognized as a “ Great College to Work For ” every year since 2015, Angelo State offers a collaborative workplace grounded in core values that guide how employees work, grow and contribute. Search Job Postings Our Core Values Integrity Diversity and Inclusion Significance Community Commitment These values are the foundation of the Ram Family and guide how we support our employees throughout their careers. With approximately 1,770 employees, Angelo State offers opportunities in a variety of areas, including teaching, information technology, athletics, student programs and administrative support. These are just a few of the roles through which employees contribute to the meaningful work that directly impacts students and strengthens the region. Whether you’re early in your career or bringing years of experience, Angelo State offers meaningful work in a supportive environment where employees play a direct role in student success and campus life. Why Work at ASU Working at Angelo State isn’t simply holding a position. It’s about belonging to a campus community that invests in its people. You’ll enjoy: A supportive campus culture rooted in shared values Stable employment within the Texas Tech University System Comprehensive benefits and work-life resources A close-knit campus community with a statewide impact Browse Employment Opportunities at ASU Explore current faculty, staff and student job openings to find the right fit for your career path. Search Job Postings Angelo State University is an equal opportunity employer. <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “ASU has everything that a big D-I school has to offer, but we’re small enough to still have a family-oriented environment. I recruit to that, because we’re not lacking anything.”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong><a href=\"/live/news/18739-challenge-accepted\">Alesha Ellis</a></strong>, Head Women’s Basketball Coach</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “Every day that I walk onto campus or step into the classroom or meet with a student, my hope is that I can make someone come alive, just as others did for me years ago.”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong><a href=\"/live/news/19135-faculty-spotlight-gayle-randall\">Dr. Gayle Randall</a></strong>, Assistant Professor of Marketing, Class of 1990 and 1991</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “If you ask anyone at ASU what keeps them here, the No. 1 answer is going to be the people.”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong><a href=\"/live/news/19716-homecoming-honoree-kevin-brooks\">Kevin Brooks</a></strong>, Head Baseball Coach</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “I am blessed to fill my days at Angelo State where we all work together to make an impact in this exceptional university that will always be my HOME.”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong><a href=\"/live/news/19135-faculty-spotlight-gayle-randall\">Dr. Gayle Randall</a></strong>, Assistant Professor of Marketing, Class of 1990 and 1991</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “I love working at ASU because I always enjoy putting live remotes on within the Houston Harte University Center for the student body to see what the radio station is about and decide if they want to peruse a radio show.”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong>Jacob Tucker</strong>, Class of 2023</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “We have caring faculty and staff, and awesome students.”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong><a href=\"/live/news/18738-biceps-and-bowties\">Dr. Jordan Daniel</a></strong>, Kinesiology</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “I enjoy the open lines of communication and the organized manner in which the administration run the business side of ASU. Being employed at a ‘well-oiled machine’ makes everyone’s job more efficient and enables faculty and staff to focus on the duties for which they were hired.”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong>Dr. Kyle Beran</strong>, Class of 1989, Chair, ASU Chemistry and Biochemistry Department</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “I love working here at ASU because we care about students, and we want them to succeed and be better.”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong>Raegan Strain</strong>, Office Coordinator, Residential Programs</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “My job at ASU as an RA gave me experience and connections to do what I do now!”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong>Jordon Perry</strong>, Class of 2014 & 2016, Operations Coordinator, ASU Residential Programs</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “What we have at ASU is really unparalleled.”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong><a href=\"/live/news/19716-homecoming-honoree-kevin-brooks\">Kevin Brooks</a></strong>, Head Baseball Coach</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “Speaking as both an ASU alumna and an employee, I bleed blue and gold. Go Rams and Rambelles!”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong>Kimberly Wirth</strong>, Class of 2005, ASU Research Librarian</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “Dr. Christine Purkiss gave me a chance to work for this amazing university, which made me realize I wanted to continue my career here. The best moment I’ve ever had was calling a student to tell them they had been admitted, and they were so excited, they cried.”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong>Danielle Plecenik</strong>, Class of 2018, ASU Admissions Counselor</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “As a research librarian, I’m dedicated to helping students adjust their research skills to a method that saves them time and brings better results. There is no better reward than when a student approaches me after a session to express appreciation for the learning experience.”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong>Kimberly Wirth</strong>, Class of 2005, ASU Research Librarian</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “I love how ASU is dedicated to our students and to helping them succeed.”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong><a href=\"/live/news/19704-homecoming-honoree-dr-tammy-stafford\">Dr. Tammy Stafford</a></strong>, Associate Clinical Professor of Nursing</p>\n  </blockquote> <blockquote class=\"quote-block--simple\">\n    <p>  “I love working for Angelo State because everyone is so nice and helpful. Taking this job was going to mean doing a lot of things I have never done before. Everyone was so welcoming and happy to help me transition into my new position as smoothly as possible.”</p>\n    <p class=\"blockquote-author\"><strong>Hannah Hoelscher</strong>, Class of 2017, ASU Admissions Counselor</p>\n  </blockquote> Angelo State in Action Our faculty and staff contribute to student success and community impact. Non-Discrimination Statement The University is committed to providing and strengthening an educational, working, and living environment where students, faculty, staff, and visitors are free from any form of unlawful discrimination. Non-Discrimination Statement Contact Us Employment 325-942-2168 hr@angelo.edu Map: Hardeman Student Services Center , Suite 202 ASU Station #11009 San Angelo, TX 76909-1009 Quick Links Faculty/Staff Job Postings About Angelo State Benefits 2601 W. Avenue N San Angelo, TX 76909 1-800-946-8627 Campus Map Contact ASU University Directory RamPort Jobs at ASU Facebook X Instagram YouTube ©2026 Angelo State University All Rights Reserved Editor Login Scroll to Top TTU System Texas Tech University TTU Health Sciences Center TTUHSC El Paso Midwestern State University Institutional Résumés ASU Privacy Policy Weather and Emergency Notifications Mental Health Services Title IX/Incident Report State of Texas Statewide Search Texas Homeland Security Texas Veterans Portal State Auditor’s Office Fraud Prevention Site Policies"
    }
  },
